          "why_it_matters": "The clarinet is the reason to pay attention here. Winograd works inside klezmer as a living dance language rather than repertory preservation, and The Barns turns that into a social event: the band, an actual dance instructor and the second night of Hanukkah all make rhythm and communal response part of the performance. The NCTA, George Mason immigration-research and local Jewish-community partnerships give the night a specific cultural frame without turning the music into a lecture.",
